builds/codex-git-admin/fix-1.md:3:1. Real bug (lib/agent.js trust detection): the live probe's worker sat on Codex's trust dialog and `wait` returned `no_start` instead of `stuck` kind trust. This variant appears when the cwd is a linked worktree / subdirectory of a repo. Exact screen (80-col pane):
builds/codex-git-admin/fix-1.md:12:  model request. Continue only if you trust these files. Your trust decision will
builds/codex-git-admin/fix-1.md:18:Add it as a fixture (tests/fixtures/agent-screens/codex-trust-subdir.txt), a test that fails on main, then fix detection. Check the installed Codex bundle for any other trust-dialog variants and cover them too.
builds/codex-git-admin/fix-1.md:19:2. The probe can't run as written: its brand-new repo always triggers Codex's trust dialog, and answering it writes Codex config (the operator's call). Change probe.sh to create its linked worktree from THIS repository (`git worktree add --detach <temp>/probe-wt HEAD`, like builds/agent-command/rig/run.mjs) so trust is inherited; keep every attempt harmless (identical bytes for commondir/gitdir/common config; config.worktree and common/hooks/<unique name> must be removed afterwards if they ever got written); remove the worktree at the end. It must not depend on the builder role: take the family as an argument, default sol.
builds/codex-git-admin/slice.out:19:Review the branch diff below for CODE CORRECTNESS only — bugs, regressions, broken edge cases, bad error handling, data-integrity issues — judged against what the branch was supposed to do: Slice at the tip of the x2 PR: Codex workers get file-level git grants (commondir/gitdir/config.worktree never writable), a private TMPDIR, sandbox pins on every launch, an ordinary-index override for split-index repos; Codex trust-dialog variants detected. Live probe with a real Codex worker: commit ok, temp write ok, every redirect denied. Already reviewed: review 2026-11-17-00-41-49-727ac2 (closed) and its fix check. No open standalone security findings on codex-git-admin.. Inspect the diff (open files as needed) BEFORE answering. Do NOT comment on product direction, scope, or style preference.
