packs/review-gate/skills/claude/code-review/SKILL.md:34:- **Portable — configure, don't fork.** The same script runs in any repo. The base branch is **auto-detected** from `origin/HEAD`, so `staging`/`master`/`develop` repos need no setup; `REVIEW_BASE=origin/<branch>` still pins it for one run. If `origin/HEAD` can't be resolved it warns loudly before falling back to `origin/main` — never a silent wrong-base review. It never writes `origin/HEAD` itself (that ref decides what the push gate trusts as the default branch): run `git remote set-head origin --auto` once to set it. One gap it can't catch: an `origin/HEAD` that is set but *stale* (the remote renamed its default branch after you cloned) resolves silently to the old branch — the run banner prints the resolved base, so check it, and re-run `git remote set-head origin --auto` if it looks wrong.
