t file as not reviewed, so the PR shows them. The operator can list more files in `coverageExempt` (globs, like `riskPaths`) or turn the defaults off with `"coverageExemptDefaults": false`: in the home config (`coverageExempt` also through `REVIEW_COVERAGE_EXEMPT`) or an untracked repo config, never a tracked one. A tracked repo config never drops these home-config values either: the home file's `coverageExempt`, `coverageExemptDefaults`, `grokMcpAllow`, `verifyCmd`, `classifier` and `base` stay in force over it. Agents don't add to the list on their own. A refusal for any other file whose diff alone is over the cap goes in the PR as a blocker for the operator, never as a shell command for them to paste.
