  "findings": [
    {
      "issue": "The file-level grants are checked for symlinks only at launch, so a worker can swap a granted leaf for a symlink during its session and have the orchestrator's later unsandboxed git write through it. A writable root on `<gitdir>/COMMIT_EDITMSG`, `index`, `HEAD` or `logs` must allow unlink and create at that path, because git itself renames `index.lock` onto `index`. A Codex worker steered by prompt injection (repo content, tool output) can therefore run `ln -sf <any operator-writable file> <gitdir>/COMMIT_EDITMSG`. Its own writes through the link stay denied, but the orchestrator's next `git commit` in that worktree opens COMMIT_EDITMSG with a plain truncating open and overwrites the target with the commit message. The same swap on `index` makes git lock and rename onto the link target, and a symlink at `logs/HEAD` gets reflog lines appended to its target. Harmed principal: the operator, whose files outside the sandbox (shared `.git/config`, shell rc files, keys) are overwritten with their own privileges. unverified — the launch-only check is read from lib/agent.js:479-488 and tests/agent-git-access.mjs; the Seatbelt and git behaviours are from knowledge, not run here, and probe.sh has no symlink-swap step. The base granted the whole admin directory, so this path predates the branch; the branch narrows it but leaves it open.",
      "file": "lib/agent.js",
      "line": "479",
      "quote": "'          for name in index index.lock HEAD HEAD.lock COMMIT_EDITMSG; do',",
      "suggestion": "Add a probe step that tries to replace COMMIT_EDITMSG and index with a symlink, to confirm or refute the sandbox half. If the swap succeeds, lstat every granted leaf (and the entries under `<gitdir>/logs`) when a Codex worker's turn ends and on close, and report a distinct tampered state instead of `done` when any is a symlink or no longer a regular file or real directory, so the orchestrator never runs git in that worktree unwarned.",
      "likelihood": 2,
      "impact": 8,
      "protected": false,
      "trigger": "A Codex worker in a linked worktree, steered by injected instructions in content it reads, runs `ln -sf <target> \"$(git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir)/COMMIT_EDITMSG\"`; the orchestrator then commits in the same worktree (for example the routine build-folder commit). No path without a hostile or injected worker reaches it.",
